    "show_share": true,
    "description": "More than 660 students in Pakistan, Kenya, Tanzania and Uganda graduated from the Aga Khan University in a live-streamed Global Convocation Ceremony that was watched by viewers around the world. The ceremony in Nairobi was attended in-person by Princess Zahra Aga Khan and saw the University commit to becoming carbon neutral in its operations by 2030. Climate scientist, author and activist Dr Peter Kalmus addressed the convocation as its chief guest.",
